<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
Author: Claude Opus 5.5 High
Date: 21-November-2026
PURPOSE: The app's privacy manifest, which the App Store requires. It says Breakdown does no tracking, contacts no
         tracking domains and collects no data, and declares the two "required reason" system interfaces the app uses:
         - Saved settings (UserDefaults, through @AppStorage and UserDefaults.standard): sound, haptics, explanations,
           the aim guide, the chosen surface and table, trick-shot progress and eight-ball best scores. Reason CA92.1:
           the app reads and writes only its own settings.
         - System uptime (ProcessInfo.systemUptime in TableCamera and ShotCamera): measures the time between frames to
           ease the camera and the Ride switch. Reason 35F9.1: elapsed time between events inside the app.
         It sits in the App folder, which Xcode's synchronized group puts in the app bundle as a resource.
         Add an entry here in the same change as any code that starts using another required-reason interface (file
         timestamps, disk space, active keyboards) or that sends anything off the device.
Edited: Claude Opus 5.5 Medium, 26-November-2026 (0.7.10 Game Center, checked and left unchanged: the game's own code
        still sends nothing and collects nothing. Game Center (App/GameCenter/GameCenter.swift) carries a signed-in
        player's daily score, streak and achievements through Apple's own service, which is Apple's data, not the
        app's, so no collected data type is declared. Its saved queue of unsent scores and its two flags are the app's
        own settings in UserDefaults, already covered by reason CA92.1.)
SRP/DRY check: Pass - the only privacy manifest in the project; the package code uses none of these interfaces.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>35F9.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
